A call stack limit on WASI (wasix-php), with a shadow-stack pad per path.

PHP checks its C stack against zend.max_allowed_stack_size and throws
"Maximum call stack size of N bytes reached" before a deep recursion in C
(serialize, json_encode, ==, var_dump, array_map or usort calling back
into PHP, __get, __toString, the compiler) overflows. configure can't run
its test when cross compiling, so it was off (php_cv_have_stack_limit=yes
in build.sh's config.site turns it on), and zend_call_stack_get() knew no
WASI stack.

What overflows first in slicc is not wasm's 8 MiB shadow stack in linear
memory but the browser's native stack, where every wasm frame sits too.
The check only sees the shadow stack, and the two disagree by path: V8
allows about 330 nested levels of usort calling itself and 2600 of
array_walk_recursive, while most C frames take a few bytes of shadow stack
or none. So:

- zend_call_stack_get() reports the shadow stack's top (__stack_high) as
  the base and at most 2 MiB as its size (2048000 bytes once
  zend.reserved_stack_size's 48 KiB is taken off);
- the C functions on each recursive path take a fixed pad of shadow stack
  (ZEND_WASI_STACK_PAD, a char array passed to an empty asm statement so
  clang keeps it), sized from that path's measured limit in V8 (Liftoff
  frames, the deepest the browser allows): the 2048000 bytes then run out
  at about 65% of the levels V8 allows on that path. execute_ex (every
  call from C back into PHP) takes 3600 bytes, sized for array_map; the
  heavier callers on top of it take their own (user sort callbacks 5744,
  preg_replace_callback 4544, SplHeap::compare 3088, __toString 2192,
  getIterator 1920, ArrayAccess 1392, __get/__set/__isset/__unset 1104,
  __destruct 864); and each check site of a recursion without a callback
  takes its own (serialize 2032, json_encode 1984, == on arrays 3280 and
  on objects 1696, var_dump 1136, debug_zval_dump 1680, count 800,
  array_walk 1040, compact 1232, array_replace_recursive 1424,
  http_build_query 2400, mbstring 1232, DOM 1552, the compiler 1504 and
  its constant folding 2048).

zend.max_allowed_stack_size still sets a different size (-d or php.ini),
and -1 turns the check off. The README has the levels each path reaches.

